                        "review": "Toxicant is a survival horror game that actually adds fresh and fun elements to the genre.  You start out as a solitary cave diver who decided to take a chance exploring a remote cave.  There were warning signs telling you it was probably not a good idea, but you entered anyway.  You end up at the bottom of the cave structure and in each level you have to find the rope and the exit to climb out and reach the next level in the cave system.  The end goal is to make it out, but if you die you have to start all over again.  The levels are randomized so you are not just repeating the same thing over and over again.  \n\nSo far, I've enjoyed my time in the game.  In addition to the rope and exit, there are other things to find in the levels, including a compass that will show you where the exit is and a map that shows you the structure of the level.  Enemy types so far have ranged from tentacles that spawn from the group, spiders that shoot green goo at you, and different zombies you have to sneak around.  I died to one of the zombies in my first run as I tried to 1v1 it bro and it won.  The menu also implies that you can level up your character as you go along.  \n\nI like the game a lot.  It's very playable in the current form and I did not find any game breaking bugs.  It's essentially an escape room roguelike and I'm not aware of any other game like it on the market.  I think the current price is more than fair and if this sounds like your type of game you can support it and enjoy it right away, unlike a lot of Early Access horror games on the market.  \n\nIf you want to read more horror game reviews, please join my Steam group - The Horror Hoard!",
